This is "NRFI Oracle" — an MLB NRFI/YRFI prediction web app.

Stack:
- Backend: Python Flask hosted on Railway
- Database: PostgreSQL hosted on Supabase (psycopg2)
- ML Model: XGBoost classifier saved as nrfi_model.pkl
- Frontend: Next.js + Tailwind CSS hosted on Vercel
- Data sources: pybaseball library + MLB Stats API (free, no key needed)

Rules:
- Always use environment variables for credentials, never hardcode them
- Use python-dotenv to load .env in all Python scripts
- Keep code simple and well-commented — the developer is learning to code
- All Python scripts should print progress updates as they run
- Flask API must use flask-cors so Vercel frontend can call it
- Always handle errors gracefully and print helpful error messages
